# Respawn near players (server/README.md "Respawn near players"). Owner, 2026-10-16: monsters must respawn even with
# players nearby. Stock Spawn::spawnMonster skips every monster of a spawn block (a boss with isIgnoringSpawnBlock
# excepted) while a player sees the spot (findPlayer) and checkSpawn starts the block's timer again, so a busy hunt
# never refills. New config spawnNearPlayers (default true): with a player in view the block still spawns when its spot
# is free (a ground, no creature, no blocking item, no protection zone) and no player the monsters see stands closer
# than spawnMinPlayerDistance sqm (default 2: never on a tile next to a player; Chebyshev, same floor, at most 7).
# The check is needed because the spawn places the monster forced (on its spot even over a creature or a blocking
# item). A respawn a player sees shows CONST_ME_TELEPORT. Spot not free or a player too close: the stock rule (bosses
# with isIgnoringSpawnBlock still spawn, silently, as before; the timer starts again). spawnNearPlayers = false: stock.
# Startup spawns and the boss path are unchanged. Lua: configKeys.SPAWN_NEAR_PLAYERS / SPAWN_MIN_PLAYER_DISTANCE.
# Built against the chain 0001-0040.
# Applies after 0001-0040.
